# The Mines of Moria

**Description:** Journey through the dark heart of the mountain, from the West Gate to the Golden Wood.
**Category:** Middle-earth
**Color:** #808080
**Character:** Aragorn
**ID:** moria
**Theme:** epic

---

## Waypoints

### The Doors of Durin
📍 -44.800, 168.100
📏 20000m

Speak friend and enter. The Watcher in the Water ripples the surface of the dark pool as the ancient stone doors swing inward.

---

### The Great Hall of Khazad-dûm
📍 -44.750, 168.200
📏 15000m

Vast pillars rise into the darkness like stone trees. The echoing footsteps of the Fellowship are the only sound in this tomb of kings.

---

### The Twenty-first Hall
📍 -44.730, 168.240
📏 12000m

A crossroads of ancient passages. Here the Fellowship rests briefly while Gandalf tries to remember the way. Three choices lie before you.

---

### Chamber of Mazarbul
📍 -44.700, 168.300
📏 8000m

The Book of Mazarbul lies in Balin's hand. 'They are coming.' Drums in the deep begin to beat, and the shadows grow long.

---

### The Bridge of Khazad-dûm
📍 -44.680, 168.350
📏 3000m

A narrow span over a bottomless abyss. 'You shall not pass!' Gandalf stands against the Balrog, light and shadow clashing on the stone.

---

### The East Gate
📍 -44.640, 168.400
📏 5000m

Sunlight streams through the broken gate. You stumble out of the darkness, grief-stricken, as the last echoes of Gandalf's fall fade behind you.

---

### Dimrill Dale
📍 -44.600, 168.450
📏 30000m

You emerge into the blinding sunlight, weeping for the fallen wizard. Mirrormere glitters below, reflecting the peaks of the Silvertine.

---

### Lothlórien
📍 -44.500, 168.500

The Golden Wood where time stands still. Galadriel welcomes you to Caras Galadhon, and the lady's mirror reveals what may be.

---
